**Asymptotic Expansions**

**19.7. Expressions in Terms of Airy Functions**

When \(a\) is large and negative, write, for \(0\leq x<\infty\)

\(x=2\sqrt{a}[\xi\qquad t=(4|a|)^{\frac{1}{2}}\)

**19.7.1**: \(\tau=-({\frac{3}{2}}\vartheta_{3})^{\dagger}\)

\(\vartheta_{3}={\frac{1}{2}}{\int_{\xi}}^{\xi}\sqrt{1-{\xi}}^{\xi}d_{\delta={ \frac{1}{4}}}\;{\rm arccos}\;\xi-{\frac{1}{4}}\xi\sqrt{1-{\xi}}^{2}\) (\(\xi\leq 1\))

**19.7.2**: \(\tau=+({\frac{3}{2}}\vartheta_{2})^{\dagger}\)

\(\vartheta_{2}={\frac{1}{2}}{\int_{1}}^{\xi}\sqrt{{\xi}^{2}-1}ds={\frac{1}{4}} \xi\sqrt{{\xi}^{2}-1}-{\frac{1}{2}}\;{\rm arccosh}\;\xi\) (\(\xi\geq 1\))

Then for \(x\geq 0\), \(a\to-\infty\)

**19.7.3**: \(U(a,\,x)\sim 2^{-{\frac{1}{2}}{\rm i}-{\rm i}\sigma}\;\left({\frac{t}{{\xi}^{2}-1}}\right)^{{ \frac{1}{4}}}{\rm Ai}(t)\)__
**19.7.4**: \(\Gamma\;({\frac{1}{2}}-a)\,V(a,\,x)\sim 2^{-{\frac{1}{2}}{\rm i}-{\rm i}\sigma}\;\Gamma\;({\frac{1}{2}}-{\frac{1}{2}}a)\,{\left({\frac{t}{{\xi}^{2}-1}}\right)^{{\frac{1}{4}}}}{\rm Bi}(t)\)__

**Table 19.3**: gives \(\tau\) as a function of \(\xi\).

